<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    In-suite perf tests (xUnit) for the M13/P1 perf suite. Slice 1 holds the murmur2 self-check (the
    automated Slice-1 gate — no broker, no Docker, no client). Slice 2 adds the Testcontainers-backed
    producer/consumer smoke (subprocess-invoking the built PerfV3 exe BY PATH under the budget config,
    v3-only gate — D10) to this same project.

    ⚠ Same-assembly collision (PLAN §1.1.1 / §4): this project references ONLY PerformanceCommon +
    Testcontainers — NOT PerfV2, NOT PerfV3, NOT ckd. A sln/project that pulled in both Confluent.Kafka
    assemblies (ours + ckd's) would collide, so the smoke launches PerfV3 as an external process by path
    (dotnet exec) instead of referencing it. PerfV2 and PerfV3 are never in one sln together.

    Docker-gated, and the skip is VISIBLE (M13/P3 item E + D-8 Option B). The M13/P1 text here used to
    say a SkippableFact package was out of the approved dependency scope, so a Docker-absent env had to
    be a silent PASS; that constraint is SUPERSEDED — the human approved Xunit.SkippableFact as a
    test-only dependency for this project. The smoke now reports a real xUnit `Skipped` when Docker is
    genuinely absent (matching pytest.skip in the Python suite), and FAILS when PERF_REQUIRE_DOCKER=True
    says Docker was supposed to be there — because a broken Docker that reads as a green tick is exactly
    the failure mode item E exists to remove.

    TFMs net8.0;net10.0 (D4 — perf never runs on net462). Testcontainers 4.14.0 ships net10.0 + net8.0
    assets. Directory.Build.props (at bindings/dotnet/) auto-applies (#nullable enable, dotnet/runtime
    code style, TreatWarningsAsErrors, strong-name signing). Kept OUT of Confluent.Kafka.sln (D4).
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>Confluent.Kafka.Performance.Tests</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Confluent.Kafka.PerformanceTests</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.14.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.3" />
    <!-- Test-only broker provisioning (Slice 2). Confined to this smoke project (STANDING CONSTRAINT 2) —
         NEVER added to the shipped src/Confluent.Kafka binding. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Testcontainers" Version="4.14.0" />
    <!-- Dynamic test skipping (M13/P3 D-8 Option B, human-approved). Test-only, confined to THIS smoke
         project (STANDING CONSTRAINT 2) — NEVER added to src/Confluent.Kafka or to
         Confluent.Kafka.UnitTests, and it does not reach the shipped package. Latest stable at the time
         of the phase; xunit.extensibility.execution resolves to the 2.9.3 already in this graph. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Xunit.SkippableFact" Version="1.5.85" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.8.2">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../PerformanceCommon/PerformanceCommon.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
